Read `docs/CONTRACT.md` before writing any code. It is the single source of truth.

## Your lane
Check which worktree you are in and stay inside it:
- `amber-app` (branch `eng/app`) → you own `app/**` and `components/**`
- `amber-data` (branch `eng/data`) → you own `data/**` and `fixtures/**`

Never edit `src/contracts`, `src/engine` or `src/compiler`. Another agent owns those and
we are working in parallel worktrees — editing outside your lane causes merge conflicts
nobody has time to resolve.

## Imports
Only ever import shared types from `@/src/contracts`. Never import from another lane's
folder.

## If you are the app lane
Build entirely against `fixtures/*.json`. No network calls, no database, no compiler
imports. The visual spec is https://claude.ai/artifact/KCK6anxRm9zuMJc67a4WUj

- Amber means UNKNOWN and nothing else, anywhere in the UI.
- Every verdict expands to BOTH citations: the trial's own criterion text and the
  sentence from the patient record.
- Precompute the elasticity sweep. Never recompute on slider drag.
- Must work at 400px width.

## If you are the data lane
Fixtures first, in the first 45 minutes — three people are blocked on them. They must
validate against the zod schemas in `src/contracts`.

Never generate patient notes with an LLM and then feed them to the extractor. That is
circular and it invalidates the evaluation. Narrative text comes from open-access
published case reports; structured records come from Synthea.

## Hard rules
- Absent fact → UNKNOWN. Stale beyond maxAgeDays → UNKNOWN. Never FAIL.
- No LLM output is ever used to score a patient.
- Commit prefixes `app:` or `data:`. Push every 30 minutes even if broken.
